Boolean membership packages a Scott-continuous map of bounded finite range together with a finite set of admissible finite values; the class is closed under the Boolean operations.

**Definition (`BooleanMemE`).** A set $U$ has Boolean membership when $U=\{x\mid f(x)\in E\}$ for some Scott-continuous $f$ with uniformly bounded finite values and a finite set $E$ of subsets of that bound.

**Theorem (`BooleanMemE.finite_Iio`).** Every initial segment $\{m\mid m<N\}$ of $\omega$ is finite.

*Proof.* It is the range of $\{0,\ldots,N-1\}$. ∎

**Theorem (`BooleanMemE.finite_subsets_lt`).** The set of subsets of $\{m\mid m<N\}$ is finite.

*Proof.* Finite powerset of a finite set. ∎

**Theorem (`BooleanMemE.ofOpen`).** Every Scott-open set has Boolean membership.

*Proof.* Take $f=\mathrm{charOpen}\,U$, bound $1$, and $E=\{0\}$; continuity and the equation $\mathrm{charOpen}\,U\,x=0\leftrightarrow x\in U$ give the representation. ∎

**Theorem (`BooleanMemE.union`).** Boolean membership is closed under binary unions.

*Proof.* Odd–even pack the two witnessing maps and collect those packed values whose even/odd parts land in the respective admissible sets. ∎

**Theorem (`BooleanMemE.inter`).** Boolean membership is closed under binary intersections.

*Proof.* The same packing, requiring both parity projections to land in the respective admissible sets. ∎

**Theorem (`BooleanMemE.compl`).** Boolean membership is closed under complements.

*Proof.* Keep the same continuous map and replace the admissible set by its relative complement inside the finite powerset bound. ∎
